# Sensitive / baseline-governance paths — only maintainers may change these.
#
# CODEOWNERS requests maintainer review automatically. The hard enforcement is the
# `sensitive-paths-guard` status check (see .github/workflows/sensitive-paths-guard.yml)
# plus a branch ruleset on `main` that requires it. Keep the two lists in sync.
#
# RETARGETED FOR sparkinfer-k3. The inherited list owned all of `bench/scripts/`, which was
# right in sparkinfer — there the harness is scoring infrastructure and the product is
# `runtime/`. Here the harness IS the deliverable: the entire Kimi K3 baseline lives in
# bench/scripts/, so owning the whole directory would gate every contribution this repo
# exists to receive.
#
# What actually determines a verdict here is narrower — the pins and the recorded
# measurements:
#
#   reference.lock   decides what every future run is scored against
#   *.sha256         decides which bytes count as the baseline weights
#   bench/results/   is the provenance check_reference_lock.py accepts for a pinned number
#
# Everything else in bench/scripts/ (the runner, the fit model, the tests) is reviewable
# like any other code.

# The pins and the measurements behind them
/bench/scripts/reference.lock        @ai-hpc
/bench/scripts/kimi_k3_*.sha256      @ai-hpc
/bench/results/                      @ai-hpc

# The PR-evaluation pipeline inherited from sparkinfer
/eval/                               @ai-hpc

# Emission weights, the frontier ledger, and CI/governance itself
/.gittensor/                         @ai-hpc
/dashboard/data.json                 @ai-hpc
/.github/                            @ai-hpc
